{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine","id":889836,"title":"Hack - Principle as God-Machine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-13T06:27:34-07:00","id":889836,"title":"Hack - Principle as God-Machine?","content":"I like crossover games. If not as a mixed party, then at least having a game where vamps, wolves, mages, lings, and the others get together and can interact in a giant sandbox, much like Chicago did. In 1e, I used New York. Now, with 2e out, I've been using a custom designed city. Anyways, with the wealth of games out, I've decided to narrow everything down to just seven game lines - Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, Changeling, Geist, and Hunter. Vampire, Werewolf, Hunter and Changeling have been finalized and Mage is being worked in to my current all-'ling plot. <br /> <br /> So, I'm turning my attention to working Promethean into the Cage now. And... I find that, from my time playing Demon, I really like using the God-Machine. I like how the angels work, how everything is interconnected, I like the focus on strange yet modern alchemies and techgnosis. Meanwhile, I find that the Principle feels... kind of soft. Its just there. It interferes with the Pilgrimage, but nothing else really stood out. I remember there was a plague angel that took revenge on people in an orgy (rapists?), but I never got a sense of what or why beyond &quot;because angelic-like beings.&quot; And I remember that, at the end of the Water of Life Chronicle, an arch-qashmal took a bunch of Prometheans to some Infrastructure, where they could use the gears to... do something, I forgot. <br /> <br /> Anyways! The point is that I think that I want to merge the God-Machine into my Promethean game and have the Principle and its qashmal become the same thing as the God-Machine and its angels instead of being separate. I've already worked on ways to fit Deva Corp into alchemists and the like. <br /> <br /> So, can anyone think of any reason why I <i>shouldn't</i> do this? That it would be bad for the game? I know that the qashmal have a separation of elipdos/flux energies that fuel evolution/mutations in the world, which doesn't seem to be a function of the GM, but I think that can be fixed with how I want to run the GM. Any other problems, ideas, thoughts, comments?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T06:45:59-07:00","id":889848,"title":"","content":"Treat the angels and the qashmalim as Ophanim and Seraphim- that is, two choirs of the same Heaven. The main difference between the Principle and the God Machine is their goals- the God Machine tries to maintain a Status Que, while the Principle leads toward change. If you decide they are the same being, than it would truly make something which more like God than each of those entities separately, a being who envelop the world toward an unknown fate, both regulating it and developing it. It would influence the relationships between prometheans and demons, either making them into bitter enemies or into the &quot;best friends&quot;- that is, as much as someone can befriend a promethean. The main adjustments that would be needed are to the atmosphere, and deciding whether qashmalim can or can not Fall, and if not than why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T06:52:13-07:00","id":889850,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is involved in evolution and growth - indeed, that's why we call it Infrastructure; building things on top of other things we built, on top of more things, etc. It maintains an oppressive Order while it does all this, but evolution and transformation is totally a thing.<br /> <br /> How exactly is that different from the Principle's change?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Falling? I'm not including Demon the Descent in my setting, so that's a moot question. Fallen angels aren't a thing here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-13-2016, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:12:48-07:00","id":889860,"title":"","content":"when you talked about merging the GM and the Principle, I assumed about mixing all of their cosmologies which may include crossover with demon, hence the Falling- but apparently this is not the case.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I didn't said the GM doesn't mutate the world- but it is not its end goal. It's goal is maintaining order, which includes regulations and transformations- it is not the Weaver from Apocalypse, which tries to keep the world in eternal stasis. But it does work toward maintaining a specific state- it doesn't try to evolve the world as an whole, or change the laws of the universe. It doesn't care about the people who work for it or serve it- everything is a tool, a cog in the machine, part of a greater order. The Principle is quit different in attitude- it seeks to bring change as an end goal. It seeks to transform the world into something else, something greater, something better or worse. It has a personal interest in prometheans achieving their Pilgrim, while it may even inspire certain individuals into making them in the first place. It isn't a chaotic force of nature- but it is not as rigid as the God Machine either. It is about adapting, changing, transforming. It doesn't act through complicated conspiracies and great facilities, but touch each individual with divine inspiration and whispers them about a new world.<br /> <br /> That is, when the two beings are separated. As a single entity, you should decide how much of the Principle is the God Machine, and what is its true &quot;end goal&quot;- Order or Change. Are the prometheans simply regulations in the great computing system which require being &quot;fixed&quot; by turning human, or are they a great potential for transforming the world and key elements in its long term plans. The God Machine and the Principle can, undoubtedly, be mixed together to the same entity- but it would require some changes from how each is presented in its own gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T00:00:00-07:00","id":891603,"title":"","content":"I'm reading your intent as being folding the Pyros and its Principle into the God-Machine, rather than splitting the difference or the reverse. So, that would make Prometheans the work of the God-Machine, and other Azothic phenomena would likewise follow from the Purpose as well. It's no difficult feat to blur angels and qashmallims, and Firestorms as excess heat or broken Infrastructure. It does turn the story of Prometheans on its head. Is the Pilgrimage part of the Purpose, or some side-effect? Do the Created call on alchemy, or is their power derived from the God-Machine's conduits? Do the Refinements and Lineages remain, and what do they achieve for the Machine? Pandorans? Are Centimani right to twist themselves from the path? What is the Machine's need of alchemy, and why does it work, and what is the point of such a difficult discipline when more powerful energies can be harnessed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:22:40-07:00","id":891719,"title":"","content":"Just throwing out my own ideas/commentary:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=891603#post891603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Pilgrimage part of the Purpose, or some side-effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think, if the G-M needed souls for some of Its Projects, then it might help to have a method to add souls into &quot;circulation&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=891603#post891603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Created call on alchemy, or is their power derived from the God-Machine's conduits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a difference? Perhaps Prometheans use some less common occult circuits than most of the G-M's tools, by virtue of their special nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=891603#post891603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Refinements and Lineages remain, and what do they achieve for the Machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Refinements are ways to study becoming human. No reason for them to vanish, I'd think. Lineages are similar to model lines, and similarly still have a role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=891603#post891603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pandorans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops? Sometimes you have unintended byproducts. After all, Cryptids exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=891603#post891603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Centimani right to twist themselves from the path?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your views of the Machine and Its projects. And if you think Humanity is worthy goal in and of itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=891603#post891603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Machine's need of alchemy, and why does it work, and what is the point of such a difficult discipline when more powerful energies can be harnessed?</div> </div> </div> </div>More Power != better. Sometimes you need the <i>right</i> tool (in this case, alchemy) to get the job done. Dynamite is stronger than a saw, but we generally don't blow up trees we need to harvest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:13:00-07:00","id":891997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=891603#post891603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading your intent as being folding the Pyros and its Principle into the God-Machine, rather than splitting the difference or the reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I'm hoping to merge them. But, by nature, it seems the GM is much more active and spread out in reality than the Principle, so it has more parts to consider, giving it more weight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, that would make Prometheans the work of the God-Machine, and other Azothic phenomena would likewise follow from the Purpose as well. </div> </div> </div> Sort of? I mean, Prometheus stole the fire from the gods, after all; in PtC, that's the demiurges stealing Azoth from the GM engines to gift it to their creations. So, not exactly &quot;work of the GM&quot; but there is a connection. I'm not entirely sure on the connection between azoth/pyros/flux and essence/ather, or how I'm going to work that in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does turn the story of Prometheans on its head. Is the Pilgrimage part of the Purpose, or some side-effect? </div> </div> </div> Not really sure what you mean by turning the story on its head. Can you clarify? <br /> <br /> As for the Pilgrimage, I've always ran it as having a Purpose behind it. The Prommies are the Created - things are created for a reason. Well, except poor Frankie - he was born only to prove that it could happen. So, there's a whole question of free will / creator-orders angle here. But then, that's a deliberate question I like to tie into Milestones. What is your Purpose? Your Mission in life?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the Created call on alchemy, or is their power derived from the God-Machine's conduits? </div> </div> </div> Alchemy. The big G-M, angels, DtD Unchained, stigmatics, fractals, and whatever monsters the GM creates are all using a form of modern alchemy based on current scientific ideas instead of Victorian era alchemy. Alchemy, at its heart, is about the spiritual implications of scientific study of the world and its laws. There's no &quot;channeling the power of God!&quot; either in the original GM or my version of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the Refinements and Lineages remain, and what do they achieve for the Machine? </div> </div> </div> Refinements are philosophies for Prometheans - they have no bearing on the divine. Lineages reflect more elemental affinities and creation patterns than they do actual lineages, so I see no reason for them to change. Do you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pandorans? </div> </div> </div> Cryptids by another name.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Centimani right to twist themselves from the path? </div> </div> </div> How does the Principle in the Promethean core feel about the Centimani? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is the Machine's need of alchemy, and why does it work, and what is the point of such a difficult discipline when more powerful energies can be harnessed? </div> </div> </div> Like I said above, alchemy is nothing more than the spiritual applications of science. If you look at modern alchemists, you'll see that they don't remain stuck in the past, but employ the use of computers, quantum mechanics, and other modern theories in their belief system. In CofD terms, alchemy is the application of science taking into account spiritual energies like Essence and pyros, the same as the term &quot;techgnostic.&quot; Some might insist that alchemy must be from an early era of science, but I don't. And Prometheans are evolving along with modern science as well, it should be noted. Unfleshed and Zeka most notably are clear examples of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T23:19:46-07:00","id":893871,"title":"","content":"The key matter for me is theme. The GM is a vast alien entity whose interests in humanity are inscrutable and faint, while the Pyros is tied specifically to human aspiration. The GM has a usefor humanity, but it's not philanthropic, to be sure. The Pyros' Principle may indeed be as opaque and soulless as the Purpose, but it engages its subjects individually and relies on human behavior to achieve its purposes, whereas the GM rides over worlds roughshod and grinds cities and nations into pulp.<br /> How this figures, replying to your points above:<br /> <br /> -Descent from the God-Machine: Right, what is the connection? The Pyros is something alive and transformative, and now it's part of the GM, an energy caught up in its geartrain or somehow turning it. It shares a Purpose. My usual take on the GM-is-the-Pyros-is-the-GM are that the Pyros represents a power source for the GM, which have now become decoupled. Both are called out as Divine forces, so it stands to reason they are related. The Pyros seeks to drive change and confront stagnation, but the GM is less defined, and doesn't drive change so much as it effects change to reap the result. Does the Pyros' function continue as a GM appendage, and is the ensuing chaos (Firestorms, Disquiet, Wastelands) something the GM actually intends?<br /> <br /> -Alchemy and Refinements: These are essentially soulworks. Promethean alchemy is classical in its conception, rather than overtly modern, and Refinements follow that conception. If you update that expectation, do the Refinements change, and how? For example, the Refinements are keyed to alchemically significant elements, but the expansion of the periodic table challenges the symbolism of, say, Copper, or Bronze. Plenty of common knowledge about various non-Refinement elements to challenge alchemical symbolism, such as the pharmacological and energy uses of Lithium, or the lifecycle of a star's elements from hydrogen to helium and beyond. Do Prometheans then view the New Dawn as some sort of superheavy metal in some hypothetical valence? And Refinements, in the original conception aren't devoid of Divine design, but represent a set of mysteries to be unlocked, and a set of powers that call on the Pyros' divine energies.<br /> <br /> -Lineage: This'll probably change in 2e, but for me Lineages were about a literal connection to the original generation of that line. That generation might have disappeared into myth, but the distinctness of each Lineage and its surrounding mythology drove home the idea that Demiurges were extraordinary men and women who were in the right time and place to birth something new into the world. However, the 2E version of it being something of a recipe (arguably, let's not argue) fits more in line with the idea of it being a pattern. But if that's the case (and I'm not up on Demon or Flowers of Hell), are these configurations accidental, and when they are not, why would a free-willed Promethean be more useful in this role than a low-ranking angel built for that purpose?<br /> <br /> -Centimani: In this function, I'd see them as Promethean Integrators. They refuse the Pilgrimage, because it makes them into mortals, where they are just grist for the GM and no longer part of a divine Purpose. So they debase their forms into mockeries, they churn up Flux, and they try and become occult matrices in themselves. Maybe the Created are conscious of this, maybe not, but if this is the case, the Prometheans are the true Fallen, rejecting their creator's designs, seeking a different end.<br /> <br /> Your conception of the GM seems a bit more spiritually alive than mine. I think I see it a great big thresher, built to harvest and consume, lacking any actual sort of consciousness, and essentially an out-of-control machine without anybody actually at the wheel. It's not so much divine as it is capable of doing a god's work, but it is ultimately a machine, built because whatever hand that fashioned it had grown tired of doing the work itself. Cults, alchemies, and other investigations into its mysteries never find any sort of actual meaning or intent behind it, because there is no longer a meaning or intent to be found. The god is gone, there's a cinder block on the gas pedal, and it's going to keep going until it breaks down or crashes into something. A less cynical version of this would be to include things like Demons and Prometheans as failsafes and exhausts, sacrificed to prevent a fatal error (a multiversal blue screen of death, perhaps). The Pyros then is some sort of repair-function meant to purge faulty parts from sabotaging the system. Or maybe it's a flaw in the system, a point of friction where heat builds up and can't escape, destined to throw the entire machine into a halted state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","user":"Verge","date":".  Edited for readability 05-19-2016, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T04:24:54-07:00","id":893939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=893871#post893871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key matter for me is theme. The GM is a vast alien entity whose interests in humanity are inscrutable and faint, while the Pyros is tied specifically to human aspiration. The GM has a usefor humanity, but it's not philanthropic, to be sure. The Pyros' Principle may indeed be as opaque and soulless as the Purpose, but it engages its subjects individually and relies on human behavior to achieve its purposes, whereas the GM rides over worlds roughshod and grinds cities and nations into pulp.</div> </div> </div> </div> The GM uses angels and Infrastructure to engage people on an individual basis. How is that different?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Descent from the God-Machine: Right, what is the connection? The Pyros is something alive and transformative, and now it's part of the GM, an energy caught up in its geartrain or somehow turning it. It shares a Purpose. My usual take on the GM-is-the-Pyros-is-the-GM are that the Pyros represents a power source for the GM, which have now become decoupled. Both are called out as Divine forces, so it stands to reason they are related. The Pyros seeks to drive change and confront stagnation, but the GM is less defined, and doesn't drive change so much as it effects change to reap the result. Does the Pyros' function continue as a GM appendage, and is the ensuing chaos (Firestorms, Disquiet, Wastelands) something the GM actually intends? </div> </div> </div> The GM, as written, doesn't have full control over Aether or its effects on creating stigmatics / cryptids. I'm currently assuming that Firestorms represent the mutations from aether that the GM has no control over. As for Disquiet/Wastelands, that's a function of Prometheans, who were created with <i>stolen</i> power. The Created are not creations of the GM. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Alchemy and Refinements: </div> </div> </div> I have no intention of touching Promethean stuff. Only Principle/GM. Why should anything dealing with Prometheans and their philosophies matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Lineage: ... However, the 2E version of it being something of a recipe (arguably, let's not argue) fits more in line with the idea of it being a pattern. But if that's the case (and I'm not up on Demon or Flowers of Hell), are these configurations accidental, and when they are not, why would a free-willed Promethean be more useful in this role than a low-ranking angel built for that purpose? </div> </div> </div> Prometheans are born from stolen power, not a creation of the GM or Principle. They are not designed according to the any supernatural's plans or missions, but human ones. Lineages exist because of human nature, not divine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your conception of the GM seems a bit more spiritually alive than mine. </div> </div> </div> The GM's purpose is deliberately left open to fill in the needs of individual chronicles. I see no need to restrict what the GM is, but rather change it depending on the needs of individual games. Pretty much the only defining features of the GM are 1) uses angels because too big for direct intervention, 2) builds Infrastructure, 3) represents Order /Fate/Destiny in some way, 4) is a conglomeration of bio-ephemeral-mechanical parts and 5) wants to stay hidden from humanity at large.<br /> <br /> Everything else is open to debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T01:05:02-07:00","id":894608,"title":"","content":"Are you asserting that Lineages are uninspired human creations as written in PtC, or just in your chronicle? In 1e terms, the former is simply not the case, and 2e isn't revealed enough to remove the miraculous from standard progenerative acts. I'm not saying you have to keep them, just that I could argue all night and week that bog standard Promethean hinges on an engaged and boisterous god-essence, and the remove of humanity from the Created is a divide that Divinity seeks to bridge. And I traded all my vigor for rancor in the Great Home Depot Hat Debacle of the day.<br /> <br /> As to why those philosophies matter is that they are reliant on phenomena that this conception entangles explicitly with the GM, rather than skirting the issue. Refinements aren't philosophies, they're patterns and praxes that yield real results. Philosophy deals with the immeasurable and the unmeasured, action and will, and the serve to spackle over the gaps that befuddle a whole understanding of existence. Refinements and the Pilgrimage are scientific, and yield predictable results (Milestones, Transmutations, Mortality), even if the variables escape isolation. That means the Refinements and alchemy as the Created understand them are literally true, and that those truths have either premises or conclusions in the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> Also, Order/Fate/Destiny: this is where the Pyros is complementary, let's say. The Machine works through plans, requires complex infrastructure, and brutally enforces its needs by whatever means. its angels do engage human-level operatives, but they also act to complete their functions, and retire only after completion or failure. Qashmallim, on the other hand, often spawn at desperately inconvenient times, are often poorly equipped to complete their missions, and their efforts are never duplicated, and sometimes there's another working at cross-purposes. The Pyros that sends them <i>only</i> has a Principle, and that's to bring about change, whether that's through emergence or dissolution. This differs from a Purpose, an intent or goal. <br /> <br /> Big question though: are these changes intended for Promethean <i>players</i>? Azoth and its journey from fungible Pyros to distinct human soul gives shape to a Promethean for the player who inhabits the character, but if no one is playing a Promethean, so much is a moot point. As a non-Promethean character, I probably wouldn't care whether or not that Osiran had clockwork heart stolen from Infrastructure. As a player, I'd be leery of a GM connection, but that's just me.<br /> <br /> (This is all in friendliness and creative feedback. Any edges or elbows are meant to sharpen distinctions, not to assert Real True Prometheanism.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T04:37:22-07:00","id":894660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/889836-hack-principle-as-god-machine?p=894608#post894608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you asserting that Lineages are uninspired human creations as written in PtC, or just in your chronicle? In 1e terms, the former is simply not the case, and 2e isn't revealed enough to remove the miraculous from standard progenerative acts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its established in 1e that Demiurges create their Prometheans by virtue of human obsession to steal the divine spark and imbue it into their creations. The tag line of the game is &quot;A Storytelling Game of Stolen Lives.&quot; Emphasis on the words steal and stolen. I see absolutely no way out of saying that humans made Prometheans.<br /> <br /> One can argue that Extemporary are an exception, and that's fine. They are an exception, not the rule.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to why those philosophies matter is that they are reliant on phenomena that this conception entangles explicitly with the GM, rather than skirting the issue. </div> </div> </div> I see nothing in the source material to suggest that the Principle was tied to the Refinements in 1e, nor in 2e's description of them. I see no reason why the two need to be entangled. At best, that can be a theory proposed by PCs, but I see no reason why it needs to be something built into things if it wasn't before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:09:00-07:00","id":894934,"title":"","content":"Humans were participants and prime movers of the original acts, but willful attempts to steal the power of the gods seems like an oversell. Each of those demiurges were attempting to create or resurrect a being, and the Pyros took an active hand in rewarding them. That is, the Pyros acquiesced, and there's little to suggest that the demiurges would have been successful had the Pyros not responded. Some of them believed they were doing gods' work, or the spirits, but doubtful that any of them had any conception of the Pyros as a distinct and responsive force, let alone supplicated it.<br /> <br /> In 2E? Azothic Memory being introduced establishes that there is a template and metric now involved, and if the Azoth is the carrier, then the Pyros is the source. Elpis tells the Promethean that there is a map, a waypoint ahead. There is a divine roadmap at play here, and no one but the Pyros has been suggested as its author. Refinements, with their confirmed, unique Milestones in 2E are part of that map, alternate routes. They have destinations, and each is expected to put the Prommie closer to the New Dawn. Wherever that came from, it did not come from the Demiurges.<br /> <br /> But I think I'm starting to see your contention. If Prometheans are the designs of men, without Divine Guidance, then the Refinements are authored the same, or are an emergent property of the Saturnine Night. Demiurges likely did not create Refinements, since they were unlikely to comprehend what they were truly making. That leaves as the source some ingrained &quot;modalities&quot; of Azoth that the Refinements take as handles. Refinements have to work on something, and my argument is those handles were meant to be there, or the New Dawn is a happy accident, and the Pilgrimage is something less than a <i>raison d'etre</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T04:10:26-07:00","id":895411,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry Verge, but you seem to be taking a number of assumptions into play here that I flat out disagree with. Your basis feels more like your personal beliefs than something cannon, so I'm going to have to pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T00:11:06-07:00","id":895956,"title":"","content":"No worries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T21:31:41-07:00","id":897557,"title":"","content":"What if the God-Machine and the Principle are the originators of the entire Lilithim and Elpidos Choirs, respectively? Something has broken, infiltrated or otherwise corrupted the God-Machine, which impaired its capacity to uphold Order. Because of this, it sends its Angels repeatedly on completed or contradictory missions instead of erasing them like the Principle does. The accumulated bugs in the minds of the God-Machine's Angels results in what we know as the Fall.<br /> <br /> These Qashmallim of Corrupted Order are known by some as Demons, but they call themselves the Unchained. Being gifted/cursed with a continuous existence but no singular purpose, they use what they remember of alchemy (they call it &quot;occult matrices&quot;) to create artificial bodies and identities. However, they cannot reach the New Dawn, and their true natures are a closely guarded secret. Not all alliances of Unchained have the same goals, so their over-all effect on the world is one of entropy and chaos.<br /> <br /> Qashmallim of the Elpidos may not reveal anything about the Principle, but perhaps the Unchained can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}